\noindent\textbf{Reading:} every chain starts from the empty portfolio (gap 88--98\%). It gets within
1\% after a few hundred windows, and the larger windows of the follow-up runs close the last step to
the optimum. The bottom of the axis (``opt.'') means the proven optimum was reached.

\paragraph{PCE versus QAOA as the window solver.} QAOA (X mixer, 4 layers, warm-started from
\texttt{characterize\_and\_validate} angles, as in notebook~00) is a good sampler. The exact window
optimum was among its 64 most likely bitstrings in \textbf{145 of 200} windows (73\%). But a
15--18-qubit window costs 2--18\,s and holds only 2 assets, against about 1\,s for a 4--6-asset PCE
window on 7--9 qubits. Larger windows escape local optima, so at equal wall time PCE wins
($-69\,397$ against $-68\,249$ after 20 minutes).


